# SFT execution status v0.115

2026-09-26. The pre-fork descriptor topology for the write-guard process
composition is implemented and locally verified. **This fixes the channel and
inherited-FD plan, but it does not yet spawn the processes; Gate 5 remains
incomplete.** No real socket, process, cgroup, pidfd, listener, payload, remote
mutation, GPU operation, inference or training occurred.

## Completed

- Six fixed local seqpacket pairs cover guardian control, parent reservation
  ledger, broker report, worker report, guardian release and listener transfer.
  All twelve endpoints require root ownership, CLOEXEC, O_RDWR, O_NONBLOCK,
  local connected seqpacket type and distinct descriptor/socket identities.
- Final ownership is exact and disjoint: controller keeps 4 endpoints, broker
  3, worker 3 and guardian watcher 2. Together they cover all 12 endpoints.
  The guardian-prefork copy keeps exactly the eight non-controller endpoints
  needed to create its two children.
- The only allowed state paths are `initial → controller`,
  `initial → guardian_prefork`, then `guardian_prefork → broker|worker|guardian_watch`.
  A nested fork child must explicitly adopt its inherited copy by matching the
  recorded immediate parent PID, single main thread and unchanged deadline.
- Endpoint access and every transition recheck process ownership, deadline and
  descriptor identity under the topology lock. External keep-FDs cannot alias
  topology descriptors.
- Every close is consumed once. Descriptor replacement is never closed as the
  original, close failures are never retried, and ambiguous socket objects stay
  retained so object destruction cannot later close a reused numeric FD.
- Snapshots are aggregate-only: counts and fixed false claims, with no FD,
  socket identity, PID, packet or exception text.

## Verification

**857 unique tests pass on CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with no failures,
errors or skips: 21 topology tests plus the previous 836 regressions. All new
runtime, clock, PID-lineage, pair, identity and close boundaries are synthetic.

Syntax/AST checks pass for the two new files on both runtimes; maximum line
length is 92 and trailing whitespace is zero. Tests used `-B`, and no bytecode
file for the new component is present. Ruff was unavailable and no replacement
was downloaded.

