## Exact next work and unchanged boundary

The next successor must execute this topology in a fully doubled private
composition: the outer controller forks and pidfd-binds the guardian; the
guardian adopts its copy, creates the cgroup lease, forks and pidfd-binds broker
and worker; and each copy closes down to its exact final set.

The controller then needs one fixed event loop for READY verification before
guardian arm, parent reservation and ACK before every broker CONTINUE, CONSUMED
verification, aggregate broker/guardian/worker reports, deadline termination
and waitid-based reaping. After that come listener/drop/seal/full-size bootstrap
integration, authenticated source closure and separately authorized Linux
native qualification.

GPU is still unnecessary. No S3 or other remote availability check was made.
Real import, training and production remain disabled.
